message: >-
  If you use this software or its archived experimental results, please cite
  the version-specific Zenodo record associated with the release.
type: software
title: "Sequence Recovery: Graph-Conditioned Reconstruction of Learning Trajectories"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
authors:
  - family-names: Khomenko
    given-names: Serhii
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7185-9101"
    affiliation: "Kharkiv National University of Radio Electronics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sergeykhomenko/sequence-recovery"
url: "https://github.com/sergeykhomenko/sequence-recovery"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software for a controlled experiment on reconstructing masked
  fragments of learning trajectories over synthetic prerequisite graphs.
  The framework compares a random baseline, Markov chains of orders one to
  five under different history budgets, and a graph-conditioned masked
  autoencoder with directional message passing and a transformer.
  It includes deterministic dataset generation, training and inference,
  recovery and prerequisite-validity metrics, archived experimental results,
  and reproducible course-level statistical analysis.
keywords:
  - learning trajectories
  - sequence reconstruction
  - prerequisite graphs
  - predicate alphabets
  - graph neural networks
  - masked autoencoder
  - Markov chains
  - reproducible research
